PS5 HDMI: VRR test 8 (hdmi.vrr_test=1)                     [ps5-bazzite-deck, test only]

Test 7 (hsgodd, from PS5 OS 13.60 dumps) brought the picture up: Sony's VSync
block is written at every mode set AFTER the DP link is trained (1047=30
6064=03 6c07=80 7214=80,02 with VRR on) and 6224=40,0f goes into
configParamFlava3Pre; the bridge signals HDMI 2.1 VRR (VTEM) itself. Still
blinking with VRR enabled. Test 8 = test 7's order, on the v1.4 candidate, with:
  - VRR offered from the sink's HDMI Forum VRR range (FreeSync block as fallback),
    the bridge in VRR mode only for modes amdgpu gives VRR,
  - runtime switches for the blinking hypotheses, in /sys/module/hdmi/parameters/,
    effective at the next mode set: vrr_ignore_msa (1), vrr_btr (1),
    vrr_vtem_md (0: 0x1050..0x1053 as VTEM MD0..MD3 = VRR_EN, Base_Vfront,
    Base_Refresh_Rate), vrr_vsif (0: AMD FreeSync InfoFrame),
  - the VSync block line in dmesg shows every value written.
Opt-in with hdmi.vrr_test=1; without it the build behaves like the candidate.
